    // A Range printed as itself: swiftc 6.1.2 prints `0..<3`
    // and `1...3`. A ONE-SIDED range prints Swift's PartialRangeFrom/Through/UpTo,
    // whose real form names the static element type
    // (`PartialRangeFrom<Int>(lowerBound: 1)`) and so cannot be reproduced without a
    // type checker - the generic parameter is dropped and the rest is byte-exact.
    if (o["__range"] === true) {
